# Example: Unfair Repeating Fault
# The control for 10-04-fault-action: the same spec with Break as a plain
# unfair action. Break, Repair, Break, Repair, ... is now a liveness
# counterexample, because nothing stops Break from recurring forever.
# Demonstrates: why fault actions need fair<fault>

action Init:
    up = True

atomic action Break:
    up = False

atomic fair action Repair:
    if not up:
        up = True

eventually always assertion StaysUp:
    return up
